# AM01 Touch Screen UI Configuration
#
# Read by odo-ui.service. Only UI_OPTS has any effect; the user and binary path
# are literal in the unit file (systemd cannot take those from the
# environment). The binary is /usr/bin/odo-ui, running as root because it needs
# /dev/fb0 and /dev/input/event*.
#
# REQUIREMENTS:
#   - Framebuffer device (/dev/fb0) -- HDMI or parallel LCD
#   - Touch input device (/dev/input/eventN)
#
# With no framebuffer present the unit is skipped rather than failed. Use
# odo-webd instead, or disable it outright: systemctl disable odo-ui

# Command-line options:
#   -fb PATH      Framebuffer device (default /dev/fb0)
#   -touch PATH   Touch input device (default /dev/input/event0)
#   -bg PATH      Background image (PNG)
#   -font PATH    Font file (TTF)
#
# Check the touch device with `evtest` if there is more than one input.
UI_OPTS="-fb /dev/fb0 -touch /dev/input/event0"
